{"base_rate":0.4631432545201669,"brier":0.17896954102920723,"bss":0.2802107322348255,"bss_hi":0.36809062045538743,"bss_lo":0.19101440365930603,"chart":{"base":[662.5,156.9],"fp":[383.2,370.5],"lead":"62,193.4 272,184.1 482,150.9 692,69.4","note":{"base":"skill 0.28 — higher than 41% of cities","fp":"low end +16pp, high end -0pp","lead":"day-1 error 1.7 °C — better than 11% of cities","rel":"promised 1% → rained 12%; promised 94% → rained 90%"},"rel":"69.7,415.3 153.2,275.3 387.4,155.8 651.3,79"},"country":"CA","deep":false,"depth":["Rain-probability calibration","Calibration curve","Seasonal split"],"ece":0.15066759388038936,"ess":485.81766850958707,"html":{"answer":"\n<h2 id=\"answer\">The short answer for Ottawa</h2>\n<div class=\"verdict\">\n<p class=\"lead\"><b>The Ottawa rain forecast is moderately skilful, though 7 points on its probability scale are off by more than chance explains.</b></p>\n<p>When it says rain is <i>near certain</i> (99%), believe about\n<b>92%</b>. When it says rain is <i>very unlikely</i>\n(0%), there is still roughly a <b>8%</b> chance.</p>\n<p class=\"muted\">Based on 719 days, 2024-04-26 to\n2026-05-31. \"Rain\" means at least 0.2 mm measured at\nMETCALFE 4.4 NNW, 22.4 km from the forecast grid point.\nSkill score 0.28, ranked 79 of\n134 &mdash; but see the rank <i>range</i>\n(50&ndash;106) before reading anything into\nthat position.</p>\n</div>\n\n<h3>What the percentages actually mean here</h3>\n<div class=\"tablewrap\">\n<table><thead><tr><th class=\"num\">It said</th><th class=\"num\">It rained</th>\n<th class=\"num\">Days</th><th>Verdict</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td class='num'>0%</td><td class='num'><b>8%</b></td><td class='num'>215</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">underpromised</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>4%</td><td class='num'><b>24%</b></td><td class='num'>66</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">underpromised</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>9%</td><td class='num'><b>41%</b></td><td class='num'>75</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">underpromised</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>20%</td><td class='num'><b>47%</b></td><td class='num'>70</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">underpromised</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>38%</td><td class='num'><b>65%</b></td><td class='num'>77</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">underpromised</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>66%</td><td class='num'><b>79%</b></td><td class='num'>72</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">underpromised</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>87%</td><td class='num'><b>87%</b></td><td class='num'>67</td><td><span class=\"tag good\">honest</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>99%</td><td class='num'><b>92%</b></td><td class='num'>77</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">overpromised</span></td></tr></tbody></table>\n</div>\n<p class=\"muted\">7 of 8 groups are further from honest than chance\nalone can explain. The rest are indistinguishable from a perfect forecast.</p>\n","card":"\n<div class=\"gcard\">\n  <p class=\"gcard-head\"><b>Ottawa</b> <span class=\"muted\">CA</span></p>\n  <p class=\"gcard-tier\"><span class=\"tag ok\">Moderately skilful</span>\n    <span class=\"muted\">7 points off by more than chance</span></p>\n  <dl class=\"gcard-stats\">\n    <div><dt>Skill score</dt><dd>0.28</dd></div>\n    <div><dt>Rank</dt><dd>50&ndash;106\n      <span class=\"muted\">of 134</span></dd></div>\n    <div><dt>Record</dt><dd>719 <span class=\"muted\">days</span></dd></div>\n  </dl>\n  <p class=\"gcard-more\"><a href=\"#answer\">The full verdict for\n    Ottawa &darr;</a></p>\n</div>","curve":"\n<h2 id=\"curve\">The calibration curve</h2>\n<p>Each dot is a group of days sharing a similar forecast. Horizontal position\nis what was promised; vertical is what happened. <b>On the dashed diagonal =\nhonest.</b> Hover any dot for its sample size.</p>\n<figure><svg viewBox=\"0 0 430 430\" width=\"100%\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Calibration curve for Ottawa\"><rect class=\"chart-plot\" x=\"58\" y=\"18\" width=\"354\" height=\"364\"/><line class=\"ch